          prompt: "In a fictional bench register, mean settled turbidity falls from 1.04 NTU at 18 mg/L to 0.47 NTU at 38 mg/L as alum, but the 34 and 38 mg/L jars are flagged as failing the trial pH floor. Which candidate dose is best within the stated constraints?",
